lse},"content_type":"application/x-tar","state":"uploaded","size":83087360,"digest":"sha256:6e01e4d5f0591796a060bda0a1357ed8cc8b801912a7d3e569ecb246764741a6","download_count":11,"created_at":"2026-07-25T06:01:35Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T06:02:23Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/Jinhojeong/vesuvius-surface-geometry-diagnostic/releases/download/patches-v2/labels.tar"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jinhojeong/vesuvius-surface-geometry-diagnostic/tarball/patches-v2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jinhojeong/vesuvius-surface-geometry-diagnostic/zipball/patches-v2","body":"The full 200-patch eval pool behind the diagnostic numbers, extended from the two samples in patches-v1. Same layout: `imagesTr/{stem}_0000.tif` is the uint8 raw-CT channel and `labelsTr/{stem}.tif` the binary GT surface label, zlib-compressed TIFF, one label per image at identical shape.\n\n| asset | contents |\n|---|---|\n| `images_s1.tar` | 162 Scroll 1 patches, raw CT |\n| `images_s4_s5.tar` | 36 Scroll 4 / PHerc1667 and 2 Scroll 5 patches, raw CT |\n| `labels.tar` | all 200 binary GT labels |\n\nBoth image tarballs unpack into `imagesTr/` and the label tarball into `labelsTr/`, so extracting all three in one directory reproduces the pool. Shapes are 172, 236 and 300 cubed in a 126 / 54 / 18 mix, plus two 170 cubed from Scroll 5. Split by scroll only because a single archive lands at 1.86 GB against the 2 GB asset limit; the CT is dense uint8 and does not compress, so the tarballs are uncompressed.\n\nThese are the patches `scripts/eval_patch.py` and `scripts/reproduce_geometry_check.py` are written against. The geometry check needs eight crops to reproduce its table, which patches-v1 could not supply.\n\nEvery pair was checked for a matching label and equal shape before packing. Data derived from Vesuvius Challenge open data (CC BY-NC 4.0).\n"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jinhojeong/vesuvius-surface-geometry-diagnostic/releases/357076319","assets_u